g; edited the copy (name→\\\"Ada L. COPYEDIT\\\", email→copy@example.com, company→\\\"Copy Corp\\\") and the source resume still showed Ada Lovelace / ada@example.com / Analytical Corp.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Session held 5 distinct resumes simultaneously: \\\"Startup CTO Application\\\" (Grace Hopper, Modern), \\\"ML Engineer Application\\\" (duplicate, Minimal), \\\"Data Scientist Resume\\\" (Minimal), plus 2 seeds. Each opened, edited and managed (create/duplicate/rename/delete) independently; deleting \\\"Product Designer Resume\\\" removed only that card.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Search \\\"mArKeTiNg\\\" returned only \\\"Marketing Manager Resume\\\" (case-insensitive); clearing the box restored all 4 resumes. Sort \\\"Oldest First\\\" → Jan 20 2024, Feb 10 2024, Feb 25 2024, Aug 27 2026; \\\"Newest First\\\" → reverse. Ordering follows creation date, not updated date (resume-1 stayed last after its updated date changed to Aug 27 2026).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No creation-date filter exists\", \"actual\": \"The dashboard exposes only a title search box, a sort dropdown (Newest/Oldest/Title A-Z/Z-A) and a New Resume button — a full DOM scan of all input/select/button elements found no date picker, date-range control or clear-date action. Typing a date (\\\"2024-02-10\\\") into the search box yields \\\"No resumes found\\\" instead of narrowing by creation date.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-9\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No date-period validation on experience entries\", \"actual\": \"Set experience start=2030-05 (future; today is Aug 2026) and end=2019-01 (before start). Both were accepted silently: no error message, no toast, no `max` attribute on the month inputs. Preview rendered \\\"May 2030 - Jan 2019\\\".\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"All experience/education date inputs are type=month; preview renders \\\"Jan 2020 - Jun 2022\\\" / \\\"Sep 2012 - Jun 2016\\\". Checking \\\"I currently work here\\\" cleared end-date value to \\\"\\\" and set disabled=true; preview showed \\\"Jan 2020 - Present\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No persistence — all resume changes are lost on reload\", \"actual\": \"Before reload the dashboard held 5 resumes (Startup CTO Application, ML Engineer Application, Data Scientist Resume, Marketing Manager, edited Software Engineer) with Product Designer deleted. After reloading http://localhost:7005/ only the 3 original seeds are present: created/duplicated/renamed resumes are gone, the deleted \\\"Product Designer Resume\\\" reappeared, and the edited \\\"Software Engineer Resume\\\" reverted to \\\"Updated Jan 20, 2024\\\". localStorage was empty throughout — state is in-memory only.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-21\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Whitespace-only rename is accepted (dashboard dialog) and rejected silently (editor)\", \"actual\": \"Dashboard card menu → Rename → entered \\\"   \\\" → Save: the dialog closed and the card title became blank (dashboard.resumes.item.v0llw4z9kb name = \\\"\\\"), with no validation message or toast. In the editor's inline title field, entering \\\"\\\" or \\\"   \\\" reverted to the previous title but produced no error/toast either.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Typing contact fields, summary text and section headings updated preview.* observables instantly with no save action; switching template Modern→Classic→Minimal re-rendered preview immediately (heading casing/layout changed).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Moving Education above Work Experience and toggling Skills visibility updated the preview instantly (no save). After navigating to the dashboard and reopening the resume, the preview still renders Summary → Academic Background → Career History → Core Competencies with Skills visible.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Edits made across editor tabs were kept without any save action; after returning to the dashboard and reopening, all edits were intact. Dashboard card for the edited \\\"Software Engineer Resume\\\" changed from \\\"Updated Jan 20, 2024\\\" to \\\"Updated Aug 27, 2026\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Minimal style preview rendered contact header, summary text, both education entries, both experience entries and both skills. After adding a long description the layout exceeded the 720px viewport (documentElement scrollHeight 1149); scrolling brought the end of the preview document (bottom at 398px) fully into view, so the complete resume stays readable.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After switching among 7 editor tabs, returning to the dashboard and reopening \\\"Data Scientist Resume\\\": all 6 contact fields, the summary, both experience entries (with long description), both education entries (incl. GPA) and both skills are still present in editor and preview.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Bidirectional isolation verified: edits in the copy (contact name/email, experience company) left the original unchanged; edits in the original (location \\\"Manchester, UK ORIGEDIT\\\", new skill \\\"OriginalOnlySkill\\\") did not appear in the copy, which still shows London, UK and skills Python/Leadership.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null